        mountCategory = "Dungeon and Raids",
        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A full weekly raid, the Spine mechanics and a rare final-chest drop can require many attempts.\n\n1. Choose legacy Normal or Heroic before entering. Heroic is useful if you also need Life-Binder's Handmaiden; LFR does not drop Blazing Drake. A different raid size does not give an extra weekly boss roll.\n\n2. Travel to the Caverns of Time in Tanaris. The 64.4,50.0 outdoor pin marks the cave entrance: follow the tunnel down into the cavern and take the Dragon Soul raid portal in the northeast of the hub. This is a physical legacy raid run, not Raid Finder.\n\n3. Kill Morchok, then Warlord Zon'ozz and Yor'sahj. Use the Wyrmrest NPC transports and portals to reach Hagara in the Eye of Eternity and return to the temple summit afterward. Speak to Thrall and finish the Twilight drake defense; stay for the dialogue until Ultraxion actually engages. Kill Ultraxion and open the Lesser Cache for a separate chance at Experiment 12-B.\n\n4. Board the Skyfire when offered and speak to the NPC to start Warmaster Blackhorn. Kill the boarding enemies and ranged Twilight Assault Drakes until Blackhorn lands, then defeat him. Speak to the crew to continue to Deathwing's back.\n\n5. For Spine, kill three Corruption tentacles and leave one alive. Stand in a tentacle hole with Grasping Tendrils while Deathwing rolls to throw away unwanted Amalgamations. Kill Corrupted Bloods, then drag one living Hideous Amalgamation across their residue until it has 9 stacks of Absorbed Blood. Heroic's revised encounter can give all 9 from one blood residue: inspect the add's stacks rather than waiting needlessly for nine bodies.\n\n6. Move that 9-stack Amalgamation against the next armor plate and kill it there. Its Nuclear Blast lifts the plate; immediately kill the exposed Burning Tendon. Repeat for all three plates. Between planned rolls, move left and right to cancel the roll warning, or remain anchored in a tentacle hole. An unanchored roll throws you off and resets the encounter.\n\n7. At the Maelstrom, speak to Thrall to begin Madness. Use the wind jumps to visit the four Aspect platforms, kill each platform's large limb and its Mutated Corruption, then return to the starting platform for Deathwing's head. Finish the encounter and open the final Greater Cache of the Aspects.\n\n8. Search the Greater Cache for Blazing Drake and use the reins if present. If absent, repeat on another character or after the weekly reset. Do not run a different size expecting another eligible Madness chest this week.",
