        areaMaps = { 412, 414 },
        itemId = 77068,
        name = "Twilight Harbinger",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 16,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - At least four weekly Madness kills plus orb bounces, Skyfire defense and a precise Spine roll sequence.\n\n1. Track Glory of the Dragon Soul Raider (6169) and Chromatic Champion (6180). Choose the character you will use for four weekly Madness kills and record which Aspect opening platform is still missing. Set legacy Raid Difficulty to Heroic so the first six required bosses also give their Heroic kill achievements.\n\n2. Travel to the Caverns of Time in Tanaris. The 64.4,50.0 outdoor pin marks the cave entrance: follow the tunnel down into the cavern and take the Dragon Soul raid portal in the northeast of the hub. This is a physical legacy raid run, not Raid Finder.\n\n3. Morchok - Don't Stand So Close to Me: defeat him quickly before Black Blood of the Earth or his other area mechanics create a failure. If in a group, spread rather than stacking everyone together. Loot him and continue to the two lower side encounters.\n\n4. Yor'sahj - Taste the Rainbow!: pull without killing him and wait for multiple ooze waves. On Heroic, allow all four oozes in each wave to reach him. During this single fight, record each simultaneous pair in HIS absorbed color buffs: Black/Yellow, Black/Blue, Red/Green and Purple/Yellow. One wave can satisfy two pairs. The live achievement tracker may not update until the kill, so do not wait forever for its checkboxes: kill him once you have personally seen all four pairs. The room's initial trash oozes do not count.\n\n5. Zon'ozz - Ping Pong Champion: let the purple Void of the Unmaking orb appear and intercept it ten times. After each bounce, follow until its center glows again before touching it for the next bounce. Keep it away from the outer walls. Two players on opposite sides can pass it back and forth; solo, chase it or use a passive pet's taunt to hold the boss aside without damage. This also works without a pet. Confirm ten Void Diffusion stacks on the ORB, then kill Zon'ozz. The current counter can cap at ten, so an eleventh visible stack is unnecessary.\n\n6. Use the Wyrmrest transport and portal to the Eye of Eternity and defeat Hagara on Heroic. Holding Hands is absent from the live mount checklist; the lightning-chain challenge is not an extra prerequisite. Return to Wyrmrest's summit and speak to Thrall for the Twilight drake defense.\n\n7. Ultraxion - Minutes to Midnight: let the encounter engage normally, then kill him before anyone can be hit by Hour of Twilight more than once. A prompt high-level kill is enough. Loot the Lesser Cache of the Aspects for the separate Experiment 12-B chance.\n\n8. Warmaster Blackhorn - Deck Defender: board the Skyfire and use ranged attacks to kill Twilight Assault Drakes as soon as they approach. Prevent their small Twilight Barrage circles from striking the ship unsoaked; helpers can cover circles while you shoot drakes. Do not confuse those small impacts with Goriona's large Twilight Onslaught. After the defense waves, kill Goriona and Blackhorn and confirm the Heroic boss credit.\n\n9. Spine - Maybe He'll Get Dizzy...: start by killing three Corruption tentacles and leaving one alive. Anchor in a dead tentacle's hole with Grasping Tendrils on the LEFT and wait for the completed left roll. Move to a right-side hole for a completed RIGHT roll, then repeat LEFT and RIGHT. You need exactly that ordered four-roll sequence during the successful attempt. If you fall off and reset, do it again from the beginning.\n\n10. For Spine, kill three Corruption tentacles and leave one alive. Stand in a tentacle hole with Grasping Tendrils while Deathwing rolls to throw away unwanted Amalgamations. Kill Corrupted Bloods, then drag one living Hideous Amalgamation across their residue until it has 9 stacks of Absorbed Blood. Heroic's revised encounter can give all 9 from one blood residue: inspect the add's stacks rather than waiting needlessly for nine bodies. Once the four achievement rolls are complete, stop causing extra rolls and begin opening the armor plates.\n\n11. Move that 9-stack Amalgamation against the next armor plate and kill it there. Its Nuclear Blast lifts the plate; immediately kill the exposed Burning Tendon. Repeat for all three plates. Between planned rolls, move left and right to cancel the roll warning, or remain anchored in a tentacle hole. An unanchored roll throws you off and resets the encounter. Watch the achievement tracker before finishing the third plate. Heroic Spine is optional for this mount; if using Normal, expect the original nine-residue collection rather than Heroic's shortened absorption.\n\n12. At Madness, choose one still-missing first platform for Chromatic Champion: Ysera, Nozdormu, Alexstrasza or Kalecgos. Thrall is on Ysera's platform. The physical order along the platform chain is Alexstrasza - Nozdormu - Ysera - Kalecgos, so Alexstrasza requires two jumps from the start.\n\n13. For the distant Alexstrasza start, jump from Ysera to Nozdormu and back BEFORE speaking to Thrall to build Carrying Winds movement stacks. Finish Thrall's start dialogue, immediately jump through Nozdormu to Alexstrasza using a speed ability, and remain there until Deathwing announces the first Aspect assault. For the other starts, move to the selected platform as soon as the dialogue allows. Do not attack the first limb instantly: wait for the assault and the platform's Mutated Corruption to engage so the opening criterion is established.\n\n14. After the chosen first-platform assault, kill that limb and Corruption, cross to the remaining platforms and kill their limbs, then return to the start and defeat Deathwing's head. Open the Greater Cache and inspect 6180 afterward to confirm which first-platform criterion was credited. Do not repeat that same opening next week unless its checkbox is still missing.\n\n15. On the SAME character, return after each weekly reset and repeat Madness with a different missing Aspect first until all four are checked. Normal and Heroic share weekly loot/progression here, so swapping difficulty does not turn this into four attempts in one week. This criterion needs at least four weekly lockouts, even when the rest of 6169 is complete.\n\n16. Review all thirteen live criteria in 6169, including the six Heroic kills through Blackhorn. Finish any missed special challenge without repeating already-complete criteria unnecessarily. When the meta completes, check the Mount Journal and reward mail for Reins of the Twilight Harbinger, then learn the mount.",
